     :statement "Slice 1's R5 harness could only measure a transcription, because the alphabet-grain R5 has no call path. R2 has one (scripts/futon2/report/war_machine.clj:5936-5937), and that changes what a slice can produce: the planted controls are wrong versions of the code the machine runs, and the range and shape claims can be checked against what the node has already written rather than only against what it would do. Later slices should ask which of the two situations their node is in before choosing a harness."}]

